{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Changed to white.</b> At first it was black and it changed to white within the affliction. And the minimum of white hair is two." "<b>Deeper than the skin of his flesh.</b> Every white appearance is deep, like the appearance of the sun which is deeper than the shadow." "<b>And he shall declare him impure.</b> He says to him: you are impure — for white hair is a sign of impurity by decree of Scripture."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:05.049480568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}